 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "What the gateware does",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "A progressive FPGA course in 20 exercises, each a small apio project (`top.v` + `pinout.pcf` + `apio.ini`), from a blinking LED to a RISC-V SoC running MicroPython, plus a complete Galaksija retro computer. It is the **original of several ULX3S resources**: the same author's ULX3S workshop [ulx3s__fpga-odysseus](https://github.com/ulx3s/fpga-odysseus) shares 10 identical files (grom CPU, i8080/Altair computer, UARTs), and the toy \"grom\" CPU found in lawrie's ULX3S and ULX4M examples is this one ([lawrie__ulx3s_examples review](lawrie__ulx3s_examples.md)). The Galaksija project is the upstream of emard__galaksija and emard__ulx3s_galaksija."
    }
   ]
  },
