  {
   "title": "Structure",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "list",
     "ordered": false,
     "items": [
      "`tutorials/`: the 20 exercises above; each directory is a standalone apio project.",
      "`projects/galaksija/`: complete retro computer (`tv80*.v`, `video.v`, `font_rom.v`, `rom_memory.v`).",
      "`tests/`: environment checks from the README.",
      "`presentation/`: workshop slides (pptx/pdf, removed from the local clone by pruning; available upstream)."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "How to build",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "As found in the README (not run here):"
    },
    {
     "type": "code",
     "lang": "bash",
     "text": "cd tutorials/02-LED\napio build      # yosys synth_ice40 -> arachne-pnr -d 5k -P sg48 -> icepack\napio sim        # opens GTKWave on the testbench, where one exists\ncd tutorials/12-RiscV/01-Simple && make   # RISC-V firmware"
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "text": "The exercises assume the FPGA101 badge (`apio.ini`: `board = fpga101`); arachne-pnr is obsolete, nextpnr-ice40 (`--up5k --package sg48`) is the modern equivalent."
    }
   ]
  },
